# struct), whose address is p — but the dereference parsed as a word read, so `str_len(*p)`, `f(**pp)`, `str_len(*w.p)`
# and `h.eq(*p)` passed the string's data pointer as the header (`str_len` 0, or a wild length), silently, on every
# target, where `var s: Str = *p;` copies the header. The whole argument at the cursor (to its `,` / `)`) is ONE
