# decision 6), so `take8(*pu)` with `pu: *U8` into `s: S8` is refused by name, as `take8(u)` is — it
# compiled and passed U8's bytes (the user's decision, 2026-10-13: refuse by name; `take8(pu)` keeps the
# 2026-10-08 pointer rule). After the argument's parse, [st, cursor) is one `* E` inside any balanced
# parentheses, nothing after it (`*pu + a` is an operator's operand), E typed `*U` by the compiler's own
